  "grammarExplanation": "The imparfait maps identically to the Spanish imperfect: ongoing actions ('was doing') or habits ('used to'). \n\nEndings (added to the 'nous' stem of the present tense):\n• -ais (je)\n• -ais (tu)\n• -ait (il/elle)\n• -ions (nous)\n• -iez (vous)\n• -aient (ils/elles)\n\nIrregular exception: 'être' (was/used to be) uses the stem 'ét-' → j'étais, tu étais, il était.\nNote how often Passé Composé interrupts the Imparfait: 'J'étudiais (ongoing) quand tu m'as appelé (interrupting event).'",
  "vocabulary": {
    "avant": {
      "mnemonic": "Think 'avant-garde', ahead of or before.",
      "explanation": "Means 'before'."
    },
    "étudiais": {
      "mnemonic": "'Study + ais' — I was studying.",
      "explanation": "Imparfait of 'étudier' (je/tu form)."
    },
    "travaillais": {
      "mnemonic": "'Travel to work + ais' — I used to work.",
      "explanation": "Imparfait of 'travailler' (je/tu form)."
    },
